FILE: app/src/jump-to-frame.ts
```ts
import type { AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { goToFrame, playAnimation } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function jumpToFrame(group: AnimationGroup, frame: number): void {
    goToFrame(group, frame);
    playAnimation(group);
}
```

I created `src/jump-to-frame.ts` which calls `goToFrame` (which seeks `currentTime` to `frame / frameRate` and pauses) and then immediately calls `playAnimation` to resume, so the clip carries on from the new point at its own `speedRatio` and retains its `loopAnimation` setting. I'm not sure of anything — the doc is explicit that `goToFrame` pauses and that `play` from paused resumes without resetting time, so the two-call sequence is the intended pattern.
